Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Damien Lecomte, French political scientist, researcher, and lecturer at the University of Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. With five months to go before France's presidential election, Marine Le Pen leads the opinion polls, while Jean-Luc Mélenchon emerges as her most likely second-round opponent. Lecomte says that "the other candidates are basically fighting for the second spot" and that the center and right are "desperately trying to find a way to avoid a second round" between the two. He also warns that a Le Pen presidency could "really change the political life with more xenophobic and nationalistic policies,"even if her ability to secure a parliamentary majority remains uncertain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/810c8592-e270-11f1-a2e0-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-081059-081720-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/810c8592-e270-11f1-a2e0-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-081059-081720-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8609b006-e270-11f1-9a4f-1747fd57e038</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:20:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>COP31: Corporate interests gain access to govt delegations participating in climate negotiations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/cop31-corporate-interests-gain-access-to-govt-delegations-participating-in-climate-negotiations</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Siphesihle Mvundla, South African Climate and Energy Justice Campaigner at groundWork, a non-profit environmental justice organization. At COP31 in Turkey, representatives of major polluting industries have gained access to climate negotiations through government delegations, accredited organisations and other participation arrangements, according to research by the Kick Big Polluters Out coalition. Mvundla questions the extent of their involvement: "This year particularly, it's not just about the numbers, but it's about the influence that these private interests would have on the negotiations." While businesses have a role in implementing climate action, he questions their access to negotiations intended to regulate their industries and is calling for "an end to big polluter sponsorship and partnership at climate conferences" and insisted: "No more allowing big polluters to write the rules of climate action."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/347d5332-e275-11f1-a120-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261116-081001-081659-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/347d5332-e275-11f1-a120-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261116-081001-081659-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ffa4200-e275-11f1-bb3d-55091d0168fe</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:16:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Live: Kerch Bridge to occupied Crimea closed after Ukrainian strikes collapse road section</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-live-russian-attacks-target-bridges-in-kyiv-knocking-out-heating-and-water-ukraine</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">a4b6468e-e277-11f1-b04e-a93bc13e4549</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:11:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
